## Framework

Use the DI framework already in the project. Default stack: **Koin**.

- Bootstrap in Application class — keep Application minimal
- Aggregate modules in a single composition root (e.g. `KoinModules`)
- Prefer constructor injection and `by inject()` over service locators

## Module organization

| Location | Contents |
|----------|----------|
| `app/di/` | App-level singles, module aggregation |
| `data/di/` | Repository + DataSource bindings |
| `domain/` | Use case factories (via app or domain DI module) |
| `presentation/<feature>/di/` | Feature ViewModels |
| `core-*/di/` | Platform and UI dependencies |

## Binding types

| Scope | Use for |
|-------|---------|
| `single` | Repositories, DataSources, managers, dispatchers |
| `factory` | UseCases (stateless, cheap to recreate) |
| `viewModel` | ViewModels |

## Rules

- Declare modules with project's standard pattern (e.g. `lazyModule { }`)
- Register every new module in the composition root
- Bind interfaces to implementations: `single<XRepository> { XRepositoryImpl(get()) }`
- Use named qualifiers for parallel instances: `named("banner_main")`
- Presentation injects use cases and repository **interfaces** — never impl classes from `:data`

## ViewModel DI example

```kotlin
val featurePresentationModule = lazyModule {
    viewModel { FeatureViewModel(get(), get()) }
}
```
